{"abstract":"Although there is a large amount of research on adoption and benefits management, we know surprisingly little about how and why managers manage adoption of enterprise systems. By conducting an interpretive case study, we explore managers’ perceptions of adoption management. Through semi-structured interviews, we uncover that two levels of management expressed surprisingly little action to influence users’ adoption towards desired benefits once the application is live. The data analysis found a mental rationalisation pattern that justified the managers’ (lack of) adoption action. We identify these ostensive and performative structures as a project-centric mindset to highlight how the rigid boundaries of project completion are prioritised, thus challenging holistic adoption management.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Falch, Cecilie Caroline","Krancher, Oliver"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776434"],"event":{"acronym":"HICSS","title":"Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Management Actions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"why managers don t manage an interpretive case study of information systems adoption management","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://hdl.handle.net/10125/107187","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776434","ids":["itu-a2e230cf-080e-4904-a7fc-820f89a5b358"],"keyword":["Adoption management","Caes Study","Management Actions","Management Justifications","Project Thinking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E7745DF086A797D38A52CA78E2215210"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://hdl.handle.net/10125/107187","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://scholarspace.manoa.hawaii.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/21ed6935-5438-43f8-8892-c7a6a4d32c9a/content","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilie Caroline","key":"falchpau","last":"Falch","locid":"d4dc2c50-a749-4f5b-a3f1-763c1dc405fb","name":"Falch, Cecilie Caroline","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oliver","key":"krancherpau","last":"Krancher","locid":"f14f4742-c9d8-4a34-b8e2-d713c3a1f437","name":"Krancher, Oliver","orcid":"0000-0003-3876-3604","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"6687-6696","place":"Honolulu","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 57th Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a2e230cf-080e-4904-a7fc-820f89a5b358"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Why Managers Don't Manage: An Interpretive Case Study of Information Systems Adoption Management","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776434","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
